  "fixture_rules": [
    "Start each independent case from fresh copies of canonical_full_record and receipts. Unless stated otherwise, input root and capture SHA use the defaults; source hashes match and comparisonRoot is root.",
    "For each batch specification, copy the canonical batch, assign a distinct valid batch directory/name and its specified created_at. Each row specification replaces the canonical rows; copy canonical row metadata, keeping complete authored steps, operations, max_calls and criterion information. Story/test overrides are exact repository-relative paths.",
    "A sent row receives a distinct valid Check UUID in request_ids and a complete matching-ID receipt. passed keeps all canonical criterion/check passes; failed uses state failed with all criterion results failed and checks passed false; unknown uses state unknown. Set the actual row.ended_at exactly to its authored sent_at numeric epoch milliseconds, overriding the copied canonical ended_at:2000; expected at fields come from these authored records, never from Code output. Set the batch lint request ID to a distinct UUID, never a Check ID.",
    "An unsent row has request_ids:[], no Check receipt referenced by the row and ended_at omitted unless specified. It otherwise keeps complete canonical Check-row metadata; state/phase/note are local display fields only. The unsent batch may have a matching lint receipt, which supplies no Check evidence.",
    "A row with test two.json and the same Story as one.json is a distinct selected test for that Story, not a second Story. Unsent duplicate rows reuse exactly the same Story/test identity. Original source selection is the sorted unique union of every row test in that batch, before removing unsent rows.",
    "intent_variants means run each case separately with explicit intent check and with intent absent. The absent-intent variant retains validSavedCheck metadata in every row. Do not infer or alter the shared legacy predicate.",
    "expected.summaries gives exact exposed saved Story rows, independent of ordering. result is the existing checkmark for pass and no verdict for false. The case does not permit an additional false/current or false/stale summary for omitted unsent or incomplete all-passing Stories.",
    "expected.capture_test_sets gives the original sets for any source captures required by evidence in the case; appMap is null. Verify full set identity, without requiring an unnecessary number of captures. Cache lifetime and key semantics stay covered by the unchanged followup fixture.",
    "Every read uses injected local filesystem/capture ports and spies on forbidden effects. No live service, sign-in, execution of a model or expected-value harvesting is permitted. All product reads retain their default saved-evidence reader and snapshot saved Runtime state before/after the read."
  ],
